      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The late‑1920s saw William Decker Johnson establish the Johnson Home Industrial School in Preston, a rare African‑American vocational school that operated until 1936.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        12
